### Smart Queue Platform — Zero Trust auth flow
###
### Run requests top to bottom with the green ▶ gutter icon. Select the
### "local" environment (dropdown, top-right of the editor) first — it sets
### {{baseUrl}} from http-client.env.json.
###
### Cookies (the httpOnly dha_token JWT) and the OTP/global variables below
### persist automatically across requests in this file for a given
### environment — that's what lets step 2 use the cookie from step 1, etc.
### No manual header wiring needed; api-gateway's ZeroTrustGlobalFilter
### injects X-User-Id/X-User-Email downstream itself once the JWT gate passes.

### 1. Register (also logs you in — sets dha_token cookie, Gate 1 passed)
# Re-running this block fails with "email taken" on a second run — switch to
# the Login block below instead once you've registered once.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "test-{{$uuid}}@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "0821234567",
  "password": "Password123",
  "province": "Western Cape"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("email", request.body.getField("email"));
    client.test("Register succeeded", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200, got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### 1b. Login instead (use this after the first successful register)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# {
#   "identifier": "{{email}}",
#   "password": "Password123"
# }

### 2. Send OTP (dev mode returns the code directly in `data`)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/send-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "{{email}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("otp", response.body.data);
    client.log("OTP received: " + response.body.data);
%}

### 3. Verify OTP → grants the 2FA gate (Redis 2fa:{userId}, 8h TTL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "{{email}}",
  "otp": "{{otp}}"
}

> {%
    client.test("OTP verified", () => {
        client.assert(response.body.data === true, "OTP verification returned false");
    });
%}

### 4. Verify SA ID number (Luhn-checked, 13 digits)
# This sample number is Luhn-valid for testing; swap for a real test ID if needed.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-id
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "saIdNumber": "9202204720082"
}

### 5. Face verify → grants the face gate (Redis face:{userId}, 4h TTL)
# Needs a base64-encoded JPEG/PNG. On Mac:
#   base64 -i photo.jpg | pbcopy
# then paste over PASTE_BASE64_IMAGE_HERE below.
# NOTE (per verification-service's current design): this compares against a
# citizen's verified ID document photo on file in document-service — if you
# haven't uploaded/verified an ID document for this account yet, expect a
# 400 with code "NO_ID_DOCUMENT" rather than a match, and that's correct
# behavior to test for too.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/face/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "imageBase64": "PASTE_BASE64_IMAGE_HERE"
}

### 6. Confirm all three gates are open — call a Gate-3 (fully protected) route
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 7. Exercise a real protected business endpoint: list branches
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/branches

### 8. Join a queue (needs a real branchId from step 7's response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/queue/join
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "branchId": 1,
  "serviceType": "ID_APPLICATION"
}

### 9. Logout (clears dha_token cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
